    <!-- ========================================================
         SECTION 8: PVP + COUNTERS
         ======================================================== -->
    <section class="content-section" id="section-pvp">
      <div class="section-label">PvP Performance and Counters</div>

      <p class="guide-prose">
        Three scorpions plus Serket create a four-unit presence that forces the enemy into a no-win targeting situation. AoE clearing the scorpions triggers three simultaneous explosions and ATK-Down stacks. Ignoring them produces 240% ATK/sec sustained board damage and backline dives. Single-targeting them one by one consumes three consecutive immunity procs at Relic Lv.4. Meanwhile, Serket dives the backline, applies a knockdown, and emerges with a shield. The enemy carry is never safe.
      </p>

      <div class="guide-section-sub">What She Does Well in PvP</div>
      <ul class="guide-strength-list">
        <li>Board clutter creates targeting confusion -- enemy AoE must choose between heroes and scorpions</li>
        <li>ATK-Down from scorpion explosions weakens every enemy DPS hero for 10 seconds</li>
        <li>Threshold heal and permanent HP buff mean burst compositions need to commit fully to kill her</li>
        <li>Backline reach pressures the enemy carry without sacrificing frontline durability</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="guide-section-sub">Counters</div>
      <div class="counter-grid">
        <div class="counter-card">
          <div class="counter-type">Heavy AoE</div>
          <div class="counter-examples">Hecate (10s channel), Skadi</div>
          <p class="counter-why">Wide damage hits Serket directly through the scorpion mass. High-volume AoE absorbs explosion value but still kills her.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="counter-card">
          <div class="counter-type">Untargetable Opener</div>
          <div class="counter-examples">Nyx</div>
          <p class="counter-why">Nyx arrives behind the backline before Serket can dive. She cannot respond to a combat-start repositioning she hasn't reached yet.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="counter-card">
          <div class="counter-type">Hard CC on Emerge</div>
          <div class="counter-examples">Any stun or knockdown landing on emerge</div>
          <p class="counter-why">Serket commits to her emerge position. A hard CC window landing precisely on emerge nullifies her knockdown and leaves her exposed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="counter-card">
          <div class="counter-type">Energy Drain</div>
          <div class="counter-examples">Pan</div>
          <p class="counter-why">Stops her ultimate cycle entirely. No scorpions means no scorpion value, no explosions, no AoE -- the entire kit structure collapses without ult access.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="counter-card">
          <div class="counter-type">Execute Threshold</div>
          <div class="counter-examples">Anubis (r20)</div>
          <p class="counter-why">Execute at below 5% HP can trigger through invincible skill windows. If her threshold heal lands her at low HP, the execute range overlaps dangerously.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="counter-card">
          <div class="counter-type">True Damage</div>
          <div class="counter-examples">Jormungandr (stored true damage state)</div>
          <p class="counter-why">Bypasses her HP-based survival math entirely. Her DR layers and immunity windows do not protect against true damage calculations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="counter-card">
          <div class="counter-type">Debuff Cleanse</div>
          <div class="counter-examples">Mengpo</div>
          <p class="counter-why">Strips ATK-Down from scorpion explosions before it takes effect, nullifying one of the key team-debuff components of her kit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

