          <div class="verdict-context">Relic Dependency</div>
          <div class="verdict-rating verdict-rating--medium">Medium-High</div>
          <div class="verdict-sub">Real spikes at Lv.3 and Lv.4</div>
        </div>
        <div class="verdict-tier-card">
          <div class="verdict-context">Investment Confidence</div>
          <div class="verdict-rating verdict-rating--medium">Medium-High</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="guide-section-sub">What She Does Well</div>
      <ul class="guide-strength-list">
        <li>Five simultaneous value layers from a single ultimate cast -- more than most heroes combine in an entire kit</li>
        <li>Self-sufficient survivability means no dedicated healer is required for her to stay alive</li>
        <li>Backline pressure without sacrificing frontline durability -- she does both roles simultaneously</li>
        <li>Punishes every enemy response to her scorpions, whether killed or ignored</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="guide-section-sub">Where She Is Limited</div>
      <ul class="guide-weakness-list">
        <li>No execute -- she chips and disrupts but relies on teammates to secure kills</li>
        <li>No combat-start opener -- first wave of enemy actives lands before she is in position</li>
        <li>Boss single-target damage is modest -- AoE spread value is largely wasted against one target</li>
        <li>Fully dependent on ultimate cycle -- energy drain opponents shut down her entire kit structure</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="guide-verdict-box guide-verdict-box--bottom">
        <span class="guide-verdict-label">Investment Recommendation</span>
        Recommended if building around Diamond faction or wanting a durable frontline carry that doubles as sustained board pressure. Relic Lv.3 and Lv.4 are the true scaling gates. Target Lv.2 as a minimum, push Lv.3 if she becomes a core pick, and commit to Lv.4 only with long-term investment confidence.
      </div>

    </section>

